Only `lib` and `test` have an owner who holds at least half the surviving lines. `.github` and the root files have none.

I counted surviving lines with `git blame -w -M`. I ignored the formatting commit `62628c0` (Fiona Formatter's reindent and quote change) and excluded dependabot. I merged Troy Goode's two emails (`<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example`) into one person. I did not run the busfactor script, because its decay-weighted commit score isn't the surviving-lines measure you asked for.

| Path | Top holder | Share of surviving lines | Owner? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/` | Troy Goode | 159/238 = 66.8% | Yes |
| `test/` | Troy Goode | 517/966 = 53.5% | Yes |
| `.github/` | Doug Wilson | 118/366 = 32.2% | No |
| Root files | Troy Goode | 134/415 = 32.3% | No |

- **`test/`:** Troy only clears 50% because of the merge. `test/` is the closest call, and Doug Wilson holds 38.7% of it.
- **`.github/`:** The rest is split across Íñigo Marquínez Prado (95 lines), Sebastian Beltran (63), Ulises Gascón (45) and Ignacio Mangas (44).
- **Root files:** Troy leads with 32.3%, followed by Doug (115) and Jon Church (72). Most of the weight is in `README.md` (277 lines), so the root is effectively a docs-and-metadata mix.

Suggested CODEOWNERS:

```
# No single owner holds >=50% of surviving lines for the root files or .github/,
# so they are left unowned on purpose.

/lib/   @<troy-goode-handle>
/test/  @<troy-goode-handle>
```

- **GitHub handle:** I don't have Troy's GitHub handle. I didn't look it up, so replace the placeholder.
- **Recent activity:** I haven't checked whether Troy is still active. If Troy has left, GitHub would request reviews from someone who can't give them.
- **Why `.github` and root are unowned:** Adding a rule for the top committer would claim ownership the history doesn't support. If you want a fallback anyway, add a `* @team` line at the top. Last match wins, so it would sit above the specific rules.
